<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Robots on Earth and in Space</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Future Exploration of Space</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop short reports on general interest subjects. Interactive: Provide feedback on narrative writing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can develop a report on robotics used in Panama and speculate on future applications (e.g., "I researched how robots are used in Panama's agriculture to automate harvesting. In the future, robots could also assist with planting and monitoring crops in remote areas.")<br>Can edit narratives on futuristic space exploration topics, focusing on detail and coherence (e.g., "I think you could make the story more interesting by adding details about the sounds and sights astronauts experience on a space mission.")<br>Can provide written feedback on reports, assessing clarity and detail (e.g., "Your report is clear, but I think you should add more specific examples, like how robots are currently used in Panama's healthcare system to assist with surgery.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; text-align: left;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Stage & Description</h3></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; text-align: left;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Activities & Teacher Actions</h3></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; text-align: left;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Estimated Date and Time</h3></th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays an image of advanced robots working in space or on a futuristic farm. Students are asked to do a "quick-write" for 3 minutes, brainstorming 3-5 sentences about "What robots will have achieved by 2050 in specific industries like agriculture or space exploration." They should try to include new vocabulary (e.g., automation, exploration, operate, collect) and the future perfect tense.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a sample sentence on the board: "By 2030, automated systems will have transformed agriculture in Panama." The teacher underlines "will have transformed" and explains it's the future perfect, used to talk about actions completed before a future point. The teacher also models the pronunciation of /r/ in "robots" and /s/ in "space" while reading the sentence, and demonstrates how to formulate a sentence using the passive voice and vocabulary like "data is collected by sensors."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'By 2030, robots are transforming industries' correct for an action finished before 2030?" (Expected answer: No, 'will have transformed' is needed.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In the sentence 'Data is collected by robots,' who is doing the collecting? The data or the robots?" (Expected answer: The robots are doing the collecting, but the sentence focuses on the data.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 8-10 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Robots on Earth and in Space".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An excerpt (approx. 100-120 words) from a scientific report or a speculative article about the current or future use of robotics in agriculture, medicine, or space exploration. The text will contain examples of the future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional, as well as target vocabulary (e.g., automated, efficient, collect, program, control, mission, research).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> To express information, ideas, opinions, and predictions in writing, showing awareness of text organization and conventions appropriate for reports and narratives, using appropriate grammatical structures (future perfect, passive voice, zero conditional) and vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the excerpt and identify the main purpose of the text (e.g., to inform, to speculate, to persuade).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students underline all instances of future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional statements.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students answer gist questions in writing: "According to the text, what will robots have achieved in space exploration by the next decade?" and "How is data typically collected in robotic operations?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 10-12 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using the future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional, integrating vocabulary related to robotics and space (robot, technology, automation, industry, agriculture, medicine, program, control, space, astronaut, mission, explore, discover, automated, efficient, useful).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with 5-7 incomplete sentences related to robots and space. Students complete them using the correct form of the future perfect, passive voice, or zero conditional, and an appropriate vocabulary word.
                        <br>Example: "By 2040, advanced robots ______ (launch) several new satellites into orbit." (Answer: will have launched)
                        <br>Example: "Significant ______ (research / collect) by the Mars rover every day." (Answer: research is collected)
                        <br>Example: "If robots ______ (program / precise), they ______ (operate / efficiently)." (Answer: are programmed precisely, operate efficiently)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Paragraph Writing):</b> Students work individually to write two short paragraphs (3-4 sentences each) based on prompts.
                        <br>Prompt 1: Describe what robots *will have achieved* in Panama's medical industry by 2035, using at least one future perfect and one passive voice sentence. Use words like *technology, diagnose, assist, repair*.
                        <br>Prompt 2: Speculate on how space exploration *is carried out* by robots and what happens *if* a robot discovers a new planet. Include at least one passive voice and one zero conditional sentence. Use words like *explore, mission, universe, equipment*.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction (Peer Checking for Accuracy):</b> Students exchange their guided paragraphs from activity 2 with a partner. Using a simple checklist, they identify if their partner used at least one future perfect, one passive voice, and one zero conditional sentence correctly, and if vocabulary is used appropriately. They provide written feedback on grammar and vocabulary usage. The teacher circulates, provides support, and encourages respectful dialogue on grammar and vocabulary choices.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 12-15 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Robots on Earth and in Space".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual Written Report</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will write a short report (approximately 150-200 words) titled "Robotics in Panama: Current Use and Future Vision." The report must:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify one specific industry in Panama (e.g., agriculture, factory, medicine) where robots are currently used.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Describe how robots are employed in that industry (using passive voice, e.g., "Crops are monitored by automated drones").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Speculate on what robots *will have achieved* in that industry by 2040, and what new applications they *will have developed* (using future perfect).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least one zero conditional statement describing a cause-effect scenario related to robotics (e.g., "If robots are programmed efficiently, production increases.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integrate at least 5-7 target vocabulary words from the list (e.g., automation, efficient, program, control, repair, useful, technology).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher will circulate, offer suggestions for vocabulary use, and prompt students to include the target grammatical structures. The pragmatic function of "participating in discussions on the use of robotics in various fields" will be integrated as students brainstorm ideas before writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 10-12 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will exchange their written reports with a different partner for peer assessment. Each student will use a simple rubric to provide written feedback on their partner's report.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer Rubric Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the report (Is the report easy to understand? Is it well-organized?)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion and correct use of Future Perfect (at least 2 instances).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion and correct use of Passive Voice (at least 2 instances).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion and correct use of Zero Conditional (at least 1 instance).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (Is there a variety of words? Are they used appropriately?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Overall detail and specific examples provided.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher collects the reports and peer feedback sheets for further review, assessing clarity and detail in feedback as per the learning outcome. The sociolinguistic competence of "offering solutions and ensuring all viewpoints are considered" is practiced during peer feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about writing reports on future technology is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One area of my writing (grammar, vocabulary, clarity) I want to improve next time is..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 5-7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did giving and receiving feedback on the reports help me understand the target grammar (future perfect, passive, zero conditional) better?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one practical application of robotics in Panama that surprised me during this lesson?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspects of the writing task worked well? Were students able to integrate the target grammar and vocabulary effectively?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next writing activity or for students struggling with specific grammatical structures?" (e.g., more sentence frames, focused mini-lessons).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The reports written today will serve as a foundation for the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), where students will summarize and present information from their reports or from classmates' reports in different formats, potentially integrating visual aids and preparing for the 21st-century skills project on robotics.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 2-3 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>